codemap 9
tour gui-model
kind data
author ai
group gui
note The Model: all the state a view can read, and the vocabulary it is written in. Tours and steps are addressed by slot - a TourSlot is a position in the map's tour list, a StepSlot a position in that tour's steps, a StepKey the pair - because that is how the map stores them and how element ids number rows; a slot is only good until the map changes, so anything kept across a change is shifted (step views) or re-found by name and StepId (history, a reload's selection) when it does. Views read the Model through &Model; its helpers here answer in slots so a view never walks the map itself. Everything per-step the reader toggles is in StepViews, keyed by StepKey, default when absent.

