note The wizard, building a tour or editing one, Model.wizard, None while none is open: the page, the kind, the start symbol, the last focus it saw (so follow_focus reacts only to a change), the outline, the refusal shown under the page, the Mode (Build, or EditTour of a named tour), what the kind, start and typed fields held when it opened (the Baseline, so escape can tell whether anything was entered) and the Derived cache: the rows on screen, the pending TourEdit or why it is invalid, and tour_edit_changes of it, rebuilt by refresh_wizard after every act, typed key, Console command, reload and re-index rather than per frame. The typed name, group, search and note live in the wizard's fields (Which::WizardName and the others), and each step note being edited in a StepNote field keyed by its row. App::wizard's acts change it, follow_focus sets its start, create_from_wizard, apply_edit and every close (cancel, opening a tour or a step of another tour, the start page) drop it (feature-build-tour, feature-edit-tour).

